From: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mttcan: make clk_set_parent failure non-fatal on T194

On Tegra194 with the upstream BPMP clock driver, clk_set_parent on
BPMP-managed clocks fails because BPMP firmware controls the clock tree
topology - runtime parent changes via CMD_CLK_SET_PARENT are policy-rejected
for CAN modules. However, PLLAON is already configured as the CAN clock
parent at boot via BPMP firmware defaults, so the kernel-side parent set
is unnecessary in the first place.

In L4T 35.x this code worked because NVIDIA's L4T BPMP driver allowed
the parent change. On upstream 6.18 BPMP it returns -EINVAL.

Make the failure a warning instead of returning ENODEV. The subsequent
clk_set_rate / clk_round_rate calls work fine because the parent is
already correct.

Without this patch:
  mttcan c310000.mttcan: unable to set CAN_CLK parent
  mttcan c310000.mttcan: probe failed

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor OOT module, T194-specific BPMP behavior]
Signed-off-by: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>

--- a/nvidia-oot/drivers/net/can/mttcan/native/m_ttcan_linux.c
+++ b/nvidia-oot/drivers/net/can/mttcan/native/m_ttcan_linux.c
@@ -1675,10 +1675,10 @@
 	}
 
 	ret = clk_set_parent(can_clk, pclk);
-	if (ret) {
-		dev_warn(priv->device, "unable to set CAN_CLK parent\n");
-		return -ENODEV;
-	}
+	if (ret)
+		dev_warn(priv->device,
+			 "unable to set CAN_CLK parent (ret=%d) - continuing, "
+			 "BPMP-managed parent already set at boot\n", ret);
 
 	new_rate = clk_round_rate(can_clk, rate);
 	if (!new_rate)
